You can add a new bitfield, say osmall, to the object struct in
obj.h.  One extra bit per item shouldn't matter even if you're
targeting low memory machines, and it would allow you to track small/
normal for a wide variety of items, not just Dragon Scale Mail.  You
could say, for example, that any armor created by a wish would be
sized correctly for the wisher.


